# Uploads, locked files, and Dev eSign (Aug 2026)

## Uploads

- There is no Letters tab. Collection letters live on **Uploads**, grouped by type (`collection_letter` or `is_collection_letter`).
- `?tab=letters` must keep redirecting to Uploads.

## Delete lock

- **Locked for everyone:** Collection Letter and POA (`poa_document`, `poa`, `poa_signed`, `power_of_attorney`).
- **Not locked:** CC Authorization (manual uploads). Signed eSign files stay undeletable via `esign_requests`, including signed CC Auth.
- Enforce in UI, `deleteOwnClientDocument` / `deleteClientDocument`, and RLS (`lock_permanent_client_document_deletes`). Check eSign protection with the **service role**, not staff RLS.

## eSign (pilot send list; Place fields Dev-only)

- Staff send UI: `role === "dev"` **or** email in `ESIGN_PILOT_EMAILS` (`lib/esign/config.ts`): Sami (`cs@`), Jessica Gonzales, Daniel M (`daniel@stellari.io`), Amanda Curry (`amanda@stellari.io`), Asim (`asim@voxtrongroup.com`), Developer. Other admins must not see Packets eSign.
- Arlington Coaching templates (`ac_welcome_packet`, `ac_cc_authorization`) are extra send cards. Qualified users can replace those two PDFs from the E-Sign section (`Upload PDF`). They do not queue FedEx and the welcome packet is stored as `client_agreement`, not `poa_signed`, so signing it does not auto-advance stage.
- Place fields stays Dev (`canPlaceEsignFields`).
- Widen staff UI **and** matching `esign_requests` / `esign_events` RLS together. Layout write stays Dev.
- Kill switch: `ESIGN_ENABLED=false` (or `OPENSIGN_ESIGN_ENABLED=false`). Unset = **on**.
- Client `/sign/[token]` + `/api/sign/*` stay public (tokenized). Middleware must allow those paths **before** auth redirects.
- Client sign links use `publicAppUrl()` (`lib/constants/business-contact.ts`). Fallback is **`https://dspcrm.vercel.app`**. Never `app.debtsupportpros.com` (no DNS). Staff **cannot** add `send.debtsupportpros.com` SPF or a `debtsupportpros.com` CRM hostname — do not keep asking for that. Reduce spam in `send-invite-email.ts`: plain text + HTML, `reply_to` support, brand in the subject, no emojis / all-caps CTAs, visible site + full link. Invites use the same Resend `FROM_EMAIL` as other CRM mail.
- Welcome Packet signed file is stored as `poa_signed`. If the client is still in Account Manager (`welcome_packet`) or Client Services when that file lands on Uploads, auto-advance them to **Awaiting Collection Letter** (safety so they are not stuck in AM). CC Auth must not auto-stage. Welcome Packet sign still queues FedEx Pending so print is not lost.
- Required review fields (`lib/esign/review-fields.ts`): CC Auth — Name, Account Manager, MID, Card 1 last 4, Card 1 amount. Amount authorized stays optional (it totals from card amounts). Welcome Packet — MID only. Cards 2–5 stay optional. Empty required fields highlight when Confirm Before Sending opens. Client name stamps in Title Case. Account Manager is **first name only**, Title Case (same as print packets).
- Print batch still uses the packet generator, not the eSign PDF.

